#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/neon.md:0
msgid ""
"Learn how to re-install snap on KDE Neon through Discover or the command "
"line, and enable Discover support for finding snaps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/neon.md:8
msgid "Install snap on KDE Neon"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/neon.md:10
msgid ""
"Snap should be installed by default on KDE Neon. In case it has been "
"removed, it can be re-installed from *Discover*, the KDE software centre "
"application. This can be found in the Application Launcher. From Discover,  "
"search for *snapd* and select **Install**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/neon.md:12
msgid ""
"It's also possible to use the *Discover* desktop application to search for "
"available snaps. To enable this feature, select on *Settings* within "
"Discover and scroll down to the *Missing Backends* section. Select "
"**Install** alongside *Discover - Snap backend*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/neon.md:14
msgid "Install from the command line"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/neon.md:16
msgid ""
"Snap can also be installed from the command line. Open the *Konsole* "
"terminal and enter the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/neon.md:18
msgid ""
"sudo apt update\n"
"sudo apt install snapd\n"
msgstr ""
